pre-existing gap (strict `param`/`result`/`type` clause ordering in an
inline `call_indirect`/`return_call_indirect` signature, unenforced by
this crate's parser, the same "text parses when the spec says it
shouldn't" class of gap several already-vendored files have) -- not
something this addendum's scope covers fixing. The 2 `assert_invalid`
not_yet_supported directives in `return_call_indirect.wast` are two more
pre-existing, unrelated validator gaps (confirmed by running the file
and inspecting which two, not assumed): one expects a return_call_
